# {{project_name}}

{{description}}

A Claude Code plugin marketplace. Each plugin lives in its own folder under `plugins/`.

## Install

In Claude Code, with the address of this repository:

```
/plugin marketplace add <owner>/<repo>
/plugin install {{plugin_name}}@{{slug}}
```

## Develop

Prerequisites: {{runtime}}, `make`, `git`.

```bash
git clone <this-repo-url>
cd {{slug}}
make setup     # checks the tools; there is nothing to install
make check     # manifest lint + tests — should be green
claude --plugin-dir plugins/{{plugin_name}}   # try a plugin from this checkout
```

## Everyday commands

| Command               | What it does                                               |
| --------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------- |
| `make lint`           | Check the marketplace and plugin manifests                 |
| `make test`           | Run the tests                                              |
| `make check`          | Everything CI runs offline — run before every PR           |
| `make validate`       | The official Claude Code validator (needs network)         |
| `make bump V=minor`   | Next version in every manifest, and a CHANGELOG section    |

## Project map

| Path                              | Purpose                                             |
| --------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------- |
| `.claude-plugin/marketplace.json` | The plugins this repository offers                  |
| `plugins/<name>/`                 | One plugin: manifest, skills, README                |
| `tests/`                          | Offline tests                                       |
| `tools/`                          | Manifest lint and version bump                      |
| `CHANGELOG.md`                    | What changed in each version                        |
| `CLAUDE.md`                       | Onboarding guide for AI coding agents               |

## Release

```bash
make bump V=minor          # or patch / major
git commit -am "chore(release): <version>" && git tag v<version>
git push --follow-tags
```

